  "note": "Election of 15 members of Portrush Urban District Council on 21 May 1952; 18 candidates for 15 seats. No party labels are printed. D. D. Fleck's vote is damaged in the OCR and is omitted; the report lists him among the fifteen elected. Figures image-read (BNL 22 May 1952 p. 5): Carson 648 and Nesbitt 575 (corrected from 643 and 675); Knox is printed '1,609' (a misprint for 609); Fleck is printed 'D. D. Flack'. The three unsuccessful candidates, Robert Adams (Craigvara), W. Browne and D. C. Close, are named without figures and are entered without votes (council-audit, Nov 2026). Losers not printed: re-checked on the British Newspaper Archive's page image of the Belfast News-Letter, 22 May 1952, p. 5 (13 Nov 2026): there were 18 candidates for 15 seats; the three not elected are named without votes.",
  "losersNotPrinted": true,
  "correctionNote": "Corrected from the page image of the Belfast News-Letter, 22 May 1952, p. 5 (council-audit, Nov 2026): the three defeated candidates the paper names, Robert Adams (Craigvara), W. Browne and D. C. Close, are now entered without votes (none are printed)."
